                <pb facs="1143" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1063"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bowen to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bowen reports that the minister for foreign affairs, by order of the
                    President of Venezuela, has filed with him a strong protest <pb facs="1144"
                        n="1064" xml:id="pg1064"/> against the act of the United States consul at
                    Port of Spain in clearing the <hi rendition="#italic">Viking</hi> for Caño
                    Colorado, characterizing it as an interference with Venezuelan commerce and an
                    infringement on Venezuelan sovereignty; that the minister states the incident is
                    serious and requests that his protest be forwarded to the Department of State at
                    Washington.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
